{
  "_id": "tg-forgive",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "say unto Joseph, Forgive, Gen. 50:17. if thou wilt forgive their sin, Ex. 32:32. forgiving iniquity and transgression and sin, Ex. 34:7. pardon our iniquity and our sin, Ex. 34:9. atonement for them, and it shall be forgiven, Lev. 4:20. sin which he hath done shall be forgiven, Lev. 19:22. Lord is … of great mercy, forgiving iniquity, Num. 14:18. it shall be forgiven them, Num. 15:25. he will not forgive your transgressions, Josh. 24:19. thou art a God ready to pardon, Neh. 9:17. whose transgression is forgiven, Ps. 32:1 (Rom. 4:7). I acknowledged my sin … and thou forgavest, Ps. 32:5. Lord, art good, and ready to forgive, Ps. 86:5. Who forgiveth all thine iniquities, Ps. 103:3. there is forgiveness with thee, Ps. 130:4. sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow, Isa. 1:18. thine iniquity is taken away, and thy sin purged, Isa. 6:7 (2 Ne. 16:7). cry unto her … that her iniquity is pardoned, Isa. 40:2. I, am he that blotteth out thy transgressions, Isa. 43:25. I will cleanse them from all their iniquity, Jer. 33:8. I will pardon them whom I reserve, Jer. 50:20. his transgressions … shall not be mentioned, Ezek. 18:22. None of his sins … shall be mentioned unto him, Ezek. 33:16. To the Lord … belong mercies and forgivenesses, Dan. 9:9. God like unto thee, that pardoneth iniquity, Micah 7:18.",
